The base $4>1$, so the exponential increases as $x$ increases.

As $x\to\infty$, $4^x\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$.

As $x\to-\infty$, $4^x\to0$ from above, so $y\to0$.

Horizontal asymptote: $y=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,xmin=-2.5,xmax=1.5,ymin=-0.8,ymax=5,samples=100,clip=false]
\addplot[black,thick,<->,domain=-2.3:1.08] {4^x};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.4,2.5) {$y=4^x$};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=north] at (axis cs:-1.5,0) {$y=0$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

First identify the behaviour of the exponential term. Its coefficient determines the direction of the unbounded end; the added constant gives the horizontal asymptote.

(a) As $x\to\infty$, $4^x\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$. As $x\to-\infty$, $4^x\to0$, so $y\to-3$ from above. Asymptote: $y=-3$.

(b) As $x\to\infty$, $5^x\to\infty$, so $y\to-\infty$. As $x\to-\infty$, $5^x\to0$, so $y\to6$ from below. Asymptote: $y=6$.

(c) As $x\to\infty$, $4^{-x}\to0$, so $y\to-2$ from above. As $x\to-\infty$, $4^{-x}\to\infty$, so $y\to\infty$. Asymptote: $y=-2$.

(d) As $x\to\infty$, $5^{-x}\to0$, so $y\to4$ from below. As $x\to-\infty$, $5^{-x}\to\infty$, so $y\to-\infty$. Asymptote: $y=4$.

The sketch shows part (d).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xtick=\empty,ytick=\empty,xmin=-1.4,xmax=3,ymin=-4,ymax=5.5,samples=100,clip=false]
\addplot[black,dashed,domain=-1.2:2.8] {4};
\addplot[black,thick,<->,domain=-0.82:2.8] {4-2*5^(-x)};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=south] at (axis cs:2,4) {$y=4$};
\node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.2,1.8) {$y=4-2(5^{-x})$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
